				230,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Output): Add DI decorator metadata to ReplaceSearchService transform\n\nThe ReplaceSearchService transform was missing the TypeScript-compiled decorator helpers (__decorate, __param) that VS Code's DI container requires to resolve constructor parameters by their @IService decorator types. Without these, IInstantiationService bound parameters positionally with no type knowledge, causing all dependencies to arrive as undefined and crashing on this.uriIdentityService.extUri.\n\nThis commit adds: the __decorate/__param runtime helpers mirrored from VS Code's compiled output, the IInstantiationService import, the instantiationService parameter storage, and the __decorate([__param(...)]) call that binds each constructor slot to its service token (IModelService, IEditorService, ITelemetryService, ILogService, IExtensionService, IFileService, IInstantiationService, IUriIdentityService). Also changed class export from `export class` to `let` + named export to match TypeScript's parameter-decorator emit shape.\n\nThe search panel now properly delegates to Mountain's search:findFiles/search:findInFiles handlers via Tauri IPC.",
			"SHA": "46eceea1004c74e6073d68561b04e3ee7694ef49"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T19:53:53Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				230,
				6
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add ReplaceSearchService transform plugin\n\nAdd a new build-pipeline transform that replaces VS Code's web-worker-\nbacked `RemoteSearchService` with a Tauri-IPC client delegating to\nMountain's `search:findFiles` / `search:findInFiles` Rust handlers.\n\nThe upstream search service uses `LocalFileSearchWorkerClient` which\ndepends on the HTML File System Access API (unavailable under\nTauri/WKWebView) and walks files without respecting `.gitignore`. This\ncaused two problems in Land: (1) the search panel showed files in the\nexplorer but the match counter stayed at 0 because no text-search backend\nran, and (2) ignored folders like `Target/` / `node_modules/` appeared\nin results.\n\nThe transform rewrites `searchService.js` with a `MountainTauriSearchProvider`\nthat invokes `MountainIPCInvoke` with the search channel name, then shapes\nthe response into `ISearchComplete`. It preserves the DI registration so\nthe workbench transparently receives the Mountain-backed implementation.\nBoth `search:findFiles` and `search:findInFiles` are `.gitignore`-aware via\nRust's `ignore::WalkBuilder` and run native (faster than the browser worker).",
			"SHA": "b769bd954a5d923805706b02221538d95cff3c60"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-27T03:36:56Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				227,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "b15b23fcc0bb6abe76c9a5368f90a6c924b6c1f0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T20:05:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				227,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add InstrumentVscodeGit transform plugin\n\nAdd the InstrumentVscodeGit transform to the build pipeline, which\ninjects `process.stdout.write('[GIT-MARK-X] ...')` diagnostic markers\ninto the bundled vscode.git extension's main.js and model.js at\nstrategic activation-pipeline points.\n\nThe markers bypass Cocoon's outputChannel routing (which is muted in\nLAND_DEV_LOG=short) to provide unambiguous progress signals during\nthe F6 diagnostic workflow. Each marker has a distinct prefix that can\nbe grepped to identify exactly where vscode.git's activation silently\nbails out, leaving the SCM viewlet empty despite the extension\nactivating within 2814-4173ms.\n\nThe transform is self-idempotent — it skips injection if the marker\nis already present, allowing safe re-runs of the build pipeline.",
			"SHA": "d70e115fe483bffb3f7391d3692c590b5e525ad6"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-26T20:04:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				225,
				5
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Expand workbench service exports + add git instrumentation\n\nExpand the ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform to export additional\nservices and classes needed by SkyBridge's in-process providers:\n\n- SCM, Debug, CustomEditor service decorators - allow SkyBridge to\n  register providers that mirror Cocoon's extension-host registrations\n  (sky://scm/*, sky://debug/*, sky://customEditor/* events)\n- Emitter, Disposable, toDisposable - required for SCM provider shim's\n  event interface (ISCMService expects onDidChange* events matching\n  vs/base/common/event.js::Emitter's shape)\n- IModelService + ILanguageService - needed to construct real ITextModel\n  for the SCM inputBox (MainThreadSCMProvider rejects null inputBox)\n- ResourceTree + IUriIdentityService - for grouped SCM repository rendering\n\nAlso add InstrumentVscodeGit, a new diagnostic transform that injects\nprocess.stdout.write('[GIT-MARK-X] ...') markers into the bundled\nvscode.git extension's main.js and model.js. This bypasses Cocoon's\noutputChannel routing (muted in LAND_DEV_LOG=short) to diagnose why\nthe SCM viewlet stays empty despite vscode.git activating within\n2814-4173ms. The last visible marker identifies the exact bail point.",
			"SHA": "a349f4ae1e12e98b33334504832d802cdbf6d3b4"
		}
	],
